  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 137 PM CST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nSfc high pressure reigns over the Mid-Atlantic states with a sfc low \nover the northern Plains. The continued influence of this high \npressure keeps us above normal through at least Saturday and \npossibly Sunday. Highs expected to be in the 60s to low 70s.\n\nA cold front is expected to come through on Sunday and bring with it \na 30-50% chance for rain. NBM has some areas of thunder but \ninstability looks to be non-existent for our area, so have removed \nthe thunder mention. QPF is still expected to be generally less than \n0.1\" overall. The cold front drops temperatures back down into the \n50s Monday and 40s Tuesday and Wednesday with abundant sfc high \npressure. The forecast becomes a lot more uncertain Wednesday onward \nwith a few model solutions being significantly different. So at this \npoint it is difficult to say what Thanksgiving may look like.",
